                                                "sense_id": "31070236-079e-32a8-bc52-79e77e07b85a",
                                                "text": "1855 Elihu Rich in Smedley et al. Occult Sci.\nThe Romans are believed to have derived meteoromancy from Etruria."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "776ee814-7ad3-4ada-a4ff-b5fa75883d56",
                                                "sense_id": "31070236-079e-32a8-bc52-79e77e07b85a",
                                                "text": "METEOROMANCY: A special branch of astromancy dealing with omens that pertain to shooting stars. Ancient Roman augurs included thunder, lightning, eclipses, and other heavenly phenomena in such divinations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c11a0d0-d11e-46b3-ad3e-d6c00eb1c73a",
